          { name: "Extreme positions on taxation or public spending", tag: "avoid", why: "Median household income of $114,821 places this district in the upper-middle class, but the 38.9% renter rate means significant income variance and cost-of-living sensitivity. Ideological purity on taxes or public budgets will alienate both affluent homeowners (who tolerate reasonable tax rates for services) and renters (who depend on public investment). The 4-point margin reflects a swing electorate; abstract tax philosophy loses to concrete answers about what services voters receive for their money." }
