          "Recognize that this district rejected cultural polarization in 2024: The 10-point Democratic margin in a 71.85% White, moderate-income district suggests voters did not vote on identity grievance. Both parties should avoid leading with divisive cultural messaging and instead emphasize competence, fiscal responsibility, and material problem-solving.",
          "Compete on fiscal credibility and government effectiveness: This is not a tax-revolt district, but it is a district skeptical of government waste. Candidates who can couple investment in education, housing, and infrastructure with a narrative of efficiency and accountability will build trust more effectively than those offering either blanket tax cuts or blank-check spending."
