          { name: "Partisan Polarization & National Party Drama", tag: "avoid", why: "The incumbent's uncontested 2024 win (100% Republican, 0% Democrat) reflects either total partisan consolidation or Democratic candidate recruitment failure—either way, a sign that district voters may be fatigued by or skeptical of partisan warfare. A challenger who leads with national party talking points risks being seen as parachuting outside grievances into a district that likely values pragmatism and local problem-solving over ideological purity tests." }
