          "Develop a credible vocational and skills-training agenda that treats non-college pathways as equally dignified and economically viable; avoid messaging that implies college is the only route to success or prosperity.",
          "Identify and campaign on 3–5 tangible local infrastructure gaps (broadband, roads, water systems, emergency services) and explain how your policies will address them in 12–36 months—specificity defeats vague partisanship.",
          "Avoid national party talking points, identity-based grievance narratives, and culture-war framings; they will be seen as tone-deaf to a district that voted entirely Republican in 2024 without organized opposition, suggesting either consensus or apathy—neither of which is moved by ideological combat."
