          { name: "Partisan Tribal Messaging", tag: "avoid", why: "The 2024 uncontested result masks the true competitive landscape heading into 2028. If opposition emerges, heavy partisan attack messaging or ideological purity tests will be ineffective in a district where $82,819 median income and 29.7% college education suggest voters are pragmatists focused on tangible outcomes—jobs, costs, services—rather than partisan identity. Candidates must lead with problem-solving, not party loyalty." }
